## Current-user resource

{{ currentUserPatchStatus }}

The snippet involved either way:

```php
{{ manualSnippet }}
```

This patcher cannot verify one prerequisite on its own: the model behind your
current-user resource must use Spatie's `Spatie\Permission\Traits\HasRoles` trait.
Add it if it isn't there yet - without it, `$this->roles` and
`$this->getAllPermissions()` don't exist on the model.

## Admin bypass (not generated, opt-in only)

This package does not generate a `Gate::before` bypass for admins - that is too
large a decision for the generator to make on every adopter's behalf. If you want
every ability to pass automatically for a super-admin, add this yourself:

```php
Gate::before(fn ($user, $ability) => $user->hasRole('super-admin') ? true : null);
```

## Default access

Only `super-admin` gets `roles.assign`, `roles.read`, and `permissions.read` by
default - see `RoleManagement::listFor()`. This is unchanged by this feature.

## Frontend

The generated frontend service layer always reads `currentUser.permissions`,
regardless of which outcome above happened. If the escape hatch was used above and
your current-user resource is never patched, every `hasPermission` call in the
generated frontend returns `false` until it is - fail closed is the deliberate
default for an authorization layer.
